VERIFY: Wire map passes end-to-end and both students explain the observed failed result before correction.
RESET: Scrap ends disposed; tools counted; tester leads and known-good cable returned separately.
PRINTED SERVICE LOG: Standard used, tool/action/why/observed rows, initial and final tester results, cable identifier, instructor initials.
SCOPE BOUNDARY: VLAN and static-route configuration are not assessed or authorized.', '{"scope":{"response":"Only the equipment named in this ticket is affected.","quality":"exact"},"timing_change":{"response":"The issue was noticed during today''s setup; no other change is confirmed.","quality":"exact"},"symptom_error":{"response":"One tester result may show an open, reversal, or split pair; the exact result depends on your assigned variant.","quality":"exact"},"environment_equipment":{"response":"Use the assigned bulk cable, connectors, crimper, visual aids, and cable tester.","quality":"exact"},"prior_troubleshooting":{"response":"No troubleshooting was attempted before the ticket was opened.","quality":"exact"},"impact_urgency":{"response":"This blocks the assigned lab station, but no production service is affected.","quality":"exact"}}'::jsonb),
  ('sc-net-f26-03', 'SETUP: Two laptops and switch; stage one equivalent fault: bad/loose cable, disabled adapter, wrong switch port, or incorrect endpoint address.
DIAGNOSTIC BRANCHES: No link -> physical; link/no neighbor -> interface/address; local works/remote fails -> network path. Do not reveal the layer.
VERIFY: Student states failed layer, discriminating test, correction, and ping/link proof.
RESET: Restore baseline cable, adapter state, port, and addressing; verify both endpoints.
PRINTED SERVICE LOG: Initial symptom, layered hypotheses, five evidence rows, final proof, and client-facing explanation.
