PRINTED SERVICE LOG: Address calculation, command purpose, before/after interface state, gateway proof, individual contribution.
SCOPE BOUNDARY: VLAN and static-route configuration are not assessed or authorized.', '{"scope":{"response":"Only the equipment named in this ticket is affected.","quality":"exact"},"timing_change":{"response":"A technician says the router was reset recently, but cannot confirm what configuration remained.","quality":"ambiguous"},"symptom_error":{"response":"The laptop reports that its configured gateway is unreachable.","quality":"exact"},"environment_equipment":{"response":"Use the assigned Cisco pod and the two designated lab laptops.","quality":"exact"},"prior_troubleshooting":{"response":"No troubleshooting was attempted before the ticket was opened.","quality":"exact"},"impact_urgency":{"response":"This blocks the assigned lab station, but no production service is affected.","quality":"exact"}}'::jsonb),
  ('sc-net-f26-08', 'SETUP: Controlled wireless/AP station or simulation plus three client cards: invalid/missing DHCP lease, incorrect DNS, and healthy wireless reference. Do not require production AP changes.
ROTATION: Lead handles client questions; hands-on role inspects client config; evidence role runs address/name tests. Every student must inspect, cable, or run a client test and record it. Rotate next week.
DIAGNOSTIC BRANCHES: DHCP failure vs DNS failure vs weak/interfered radio path. User actions are not proof.
VERIFY: Lease/effective settings, IP ping, name lookup, and signal observation identify separate fault domains.
RESET: Forget lab SSID if required, restore automatic addressing/DNS, return AP and clients to baseline.
PRINTED SERVICE LOG: Per-client symptom matrix, ordered tests, evidence-to-layer conclusion, escalation/recommendation.
