  ('sc-hw-f26-05', 'PREPARATION: Review power-path diagram, connector identification, ESD, discharge wait, and stop-work conditions.
EQUIPMENT: One proven bench system per pair, outlet/power strip, known-good cord, PSU tester, known-good PSU, flashlight, ESD mat. Multimeter use only at instructor-approved external test points.
SETUP: Stage one equivalent safe fault: switched-off strip/PSU, loose AC lead, disconnected 24-pin ATX, disconnected CPU power, or front-panel start lead on wrong pins. System is de-energized before staging.
ROLES: One student leads communication and records the power path; the other performs hands-on tests. Both must inspect/connect and verify; rotate next lab.
DIAGNOSTIC BRANCHES: No AC input; AC present/no standby; standby present/no start signal; start/no POST. Require a discriminating observation before substitution.
VERIFY: Correct connector/state, safe startup, stable fans, and successful POST/firmware entry.
RESET: Shut down, disconnect AC, discharge, restore sealed baseline card, inventory known-good items, and independently recheck start.
SIGN-OFF: Safe handling, stated power-path evidence, POST proof, and baseline reset.
PRINTED SERVICE LOG: Initial symptom, safety step, power-path hypotheses, tool/action/why/observed rows, root cause, POST proof, personal contribution, instructor initials.
SCOPE BOUNDARY: Do not open a power supply, bypass safety controls, install an operating system, or change drivers.', '{"scope":{"response":"Only the assigned open-bench computer and listed accessories are in scope.","quality":"exact"},"timing_change":{"response":"I moved the bench and wiped around the cables shortly before it stopped starting.","quality":"exact"},"symptom_error":{"response":"There is no fan movement, indicator, or POST response.","quality":"exact"},"environment_equipment":{"response":"Use the assigned ESD mat, parts set, known-good comparison parts, and approved test tools.","quality":"exact"},"prior_troubleshooting":{"response":"I pressed the power control several times and pushed on a few connectors without labeling them.","quality":"ambiguous"},"impact_urgency":{"response":"The assigned training station is unavailable, but no production system is affected.","quality":"exact"}}'::jsonb),
  ('sc-hw-f26-06', 'PREPARATION: Manufacturer lookup for board memory slots and POST indicators; review ESD and de-energized reseating.
EQUIPMENT: Proven bench system, speaker/diagnostic LEDs if available, compatible RAM, one labeled known-good module, display, ESD mat.
SETUP: Stage one safe variant: partially seated module, module in nonpreferred single-DIMM slot, incompatible/mismatched pair, contaminated contact simulation card (do not damage contacts), or display path masking a successful POST.
ROLES: Each student performs one de-energized memory configuration and independently interprets one POST observation.
DIAGNOSTIC BRANCHES: No POST indication; memory-specific indication; successful POST/no display; intermittent restart. Research exact board documentation before concluding.
VERIFY: Repeatable POST, firmware reports expected memory amount/channel, and two cold starts succeed.
RESET: Power off/discharge, reinstall baseline RAM in documented slots, remove staged item, record kit inventory, cold-start check.
SIGN-OFF: Safe reseating, evidence-to-diagnosis reasoning, memory detection, and reset.
PRINTED SERVICE LOG: Manufacturer source/search, POST evidence, slot diagram, discriminating tests, final firmware memory result, personal contribution.
SCOPE BOUNDARY: Do not open a power supply, bypass safety controls, install an operating system, or change drivers.', '{"scope":{"response":"Motherboard, installed memory, display path, and POST indicators are in scope; storage and operating system are not.","quality":"exact"},"timing_change":{"response":"The symptom was noticed at the start of today''s check; no confirmed change is documented.","quality":"exact"},"symptom_error":{"response":"It powers on, but the display stays blank. I heard a pattern once but did not count it carefully.","quality":"ambiguous"},"environment_equipment":{"response":"Use the assigned ESD mat, parts set, known-good comparison parts, and approved test tools.","quality":"exact"},"prior_troubleshooting":{"response":"I removed and reinstalled memory without checking the motherboard slot guidance.","quality":"exact"},"impact_urgency":{"response":"The assigned training station is unavailable, but no production system is affected.","quality":"exact"}}'::jsonb),
  ('sc-hw-f26-07', 'PREPARATION: Identify SATA data/power and available motherboard storage interfaces; research assigned board/device compatibility.
EQUIPMENT: Proven bench system, assigned SSD, known-good SATA data lead, known-good power branch, spare compatible SSD, ESD mat.
SETUP: Stage one equivalent fault: missing data lead, missing power, failed/loose data lead, disabled/incorrect firmware port setting where safely supported, or incompatible-device card requiring escalation rather than installation.
ROLES: Individual ticket. Instructor may pair students only for observation; each student performs and records their own installation/test.
DIAGNOSTIC BRANCHES: No power/physical detection; cable/port path; device substitution; compatibility/firmware boundary. No OS, driver, formatting, or data-recovery work.
VERIFY: Device identified by correct model/capacity in firmware through two cold starts; compatibility source recorded.
RESET: De-energize, restore baseline device/cables/firmware setting, return known-good items separately, confirm baseline detection.
SIGN-OFF: Correct connectors, firmware proof, compatibility reasoning, and reset.
PRINTED SERVICE LOG: Asset/model, manufacturer source, before/after firmware evidence, cable/port/device tests, conclusion or escalation, instructor initials.
SCOPE BOUNDARY: Do not open a power supply, bypass safety controls, install an operating system, or change drivers.', '{"scope":{"response":"Only the assigned open-bench computer and listed accessories are in scope.","quality":"exact"},"timing_change":{"response":"The symptom began immediately after the storage device was installed.","quality":"exact"},"symptom_error":{"response":"The device is absent from the firmware storage list.","quality":"exact"},"environment_equipment":{"response":"Use the assigned ESD mat, parts set, known-good comparison parts, and approved test tools.","quality":"exact"},"prior_troubleshooting":{"response":"Someone moved both the data and power cables, but did not test either cable separately.","quality":"ambiguous"},"impact_urgency":{"response":"The assigned training station is unavailable, but no production system is affected.","quality":"exact"}}'::jsonb),
  ('sc-hw-f26-08', 'PREPARATION: Review display paths, onboard versus discrete outputs, port types, safe cleaning, and fan restraint.
EQUIPMENT: Proven bench system, monitor, known-good display cable, keyboard/mouse, USB test device, flashlight, ESD-safe brush, approved compressed air.
SETUP: Stage two independent safe faults: wrong monitor input/loose display cable/inactive onboard output plus bad peripheral/loose USB path. Add visible dust only where it can be cleaned without opening a PSU.
ROLES: Each student owns one fault branch, then cross-verifies the other''s result and participates in reset.
DIAGNOSTIC BRANCHES: Confirm POST first; display power/input/cable/output/GPU; peripheral/device/port; maintenance observation. Do not collapse all symptoms into one diagnosis.
VERIFY: Stable firmware display, repeated keyboard/mouse/USB response, fans unobstructed, and two restarts.
RESET: De-energize, restore baseline cable/input/port, remove staged peripheral, clean work area, count accessories, verify baseline.
SIGN-OFF: Safe cleaning, independent fault evidence, stable final state, and reset.
PRINTED SERVICE LOG: Separate hypothesis/evidence chain for each fault, maintenance action and reason, known-good substitutions, final verification, personal role.
SCOPE BOUNDARY: Do not open a power supply, bypass safety controls, install an operating system, or change drivers.', '{"scope":{"response":"Display, video connection, keyboard/mouse, external ports, cooling path, and visible dust are in scope.","quality":"exact"},"timing_change":{"response":"The desk was rearranged recently, but I cannot say whether the problem began before or after that.","quality":"ambiguous"},"symptom_error":{"response":"The display reports no signal; one USB peripheral intermittently loses power.","quality":"exact"},"environment_equipment":{"response":"Use the assigned ESD mat, parts set, known-good comparison parts, and approved test tools.","quality":"exact"},"prior_troubleshooting":{"response":"I moved the display cable to another connector and used compressed air very close to a fan.","quality":"mistaken"},"impact_urgency":{"response":"The assigned training station is unavailable, but no production system is affected.","quality":"exact"}}'::jsonb),
  ('sc-hw-f26-09', 'PREPARATION: Students receive a model/serial card and must plan manufacturer searches before hands-on work.
EQUIPMENT: Proven bench system, labeled known-good PSU/RAM/display/storage leads, POST reference, flashlight, ESD mat.
SETUP: Stage one ambiguous but safe variant: CPU power loose, RAM marginally seated, display on inactive output, SATA data loose, or front-panel lead shifted. Client history intentionally mentions multiple symptoms but one current root cause.
ROLES: Individual assessment. A peer may act as client or observer but may not touch the system or supply the diagnosis.
DIAGNOSTIC BRANCHES: Preserve current symptom; power checkpoint; POST checkpoint; display; firmware inventory; manufacturer/compatibility; known-good substitution; escalate on damage, unsafe condition, or unresolved evidence.
VERIFY: Three cold starts, stable firmware inventory for CPU/RAM/storage, display/peripheral response, and root cause tied to evidence.
RESET: De-energize, restore baseline, remove all known-good/staged items, reconcile kit checklist, independent instructor cold start.
SIGN-OFF: Communication, triage path, justified conclusion/escalation, stable verification, and reset.
PRINTED SERVICE LOG: Client claim versus observed state, ranked hypotheses, five discriminating tests, manufacturer source/search/result, repeated proof, next-technician handoff.
SCOPE BOUNDARY: Do not open a power supply, bypass safety controls, install an operating system, or change drivers.', '{"scope":{"response":"Power, board connections, memory, display path, and storage detection are in scope; no operating-system work is authorized.","quality":"exact"},"timing_change":{"response":"Several parts were moved between benches over the last two sessions, but there is no reliable change record.","quality":"ambiguous"},"symptom_error":{"response":"The symptom is inconsistent: no power, no display, or missing storage was reported at different times.","quality":"ambiguous"},"environment_equipment":{"response":"Use the assigned ESD mat, parts set, known-good comparison parts, and approved test tools.","quality":"exact"},"prior_troubleshooting":{"response":"I swapped the board, memory, and power supply together, and it worked once, so I blamed the motherboard.","quality":"mistaken"},"impact_urgency":{"response":"The assigned training station is unavailable, but no production system is affected.","quality":"exact"}}'::jsonb),
  ('sc-hw-f26-final-a', 'PREPARATION: Number twelve complete caseless kits; verify compatibility and baseline; seal variant A. Students may use printed books and manufacturer resources.
